### Purpose: Tutor API testing flow (VS Code REST Client).
### Flow notes:
### - Paste `tutorId` and `subjectId` from the admin flow.
### - Use this after tutor email verification is completed.
### Environment:
### - Select "local" in VS Code REST Client environments (from .vscode/settings.json).

### Tutor login
# @name tutorLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{tutorEmail}}",
  "password": "{{tutorPassword}}"
}

###

@tutorToken = {{tutorLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Tutor adds subject to self
POST {{baseUrl}}/tutors/{{tutorId}}/subjects
Authorization: Bearer {{tutorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectId": "{{subjectId}}"
}

### Tutor sets weekday availability
# @name updateWeekdayAvailability
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tutors/{{tutorId}}/weekday-availability
Authorization: Bearer {{tutorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "weekdays": [
    { "weekday": 1, "isAvailable": true },
    { "weekday": 3, "isAvailable": true }
  ]
}

### Tutor confirms lesson completion (use after scheduled end time)
@lessonId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/lessons/{{lessonId}}/confirm/tutor
Authorization: Bearer {{tutorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completed": true,
  "note": "Student was prepared"
}
